So when Bob has his transaction, it's got Alice's signature.

23
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:48,000
He doesn't store his own because he can just compute it quickly.

24
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,240
So the two coins that go to Alice go to her in the clear, however, the eight coins that

25
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:57,960
Bob gets for himself, he has to wait a hundred blocks.

26
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:05,920
During the hundred blocks, Alice can sign if she has Bob's revocation key.

27
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:12,840
Okay, so that's the basic idea of these outputs and then you construct these.

28
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:19,360
So when I say Alice, one Bitcoin, Bob, nine Bitcoin, it's of the format in these, right?

